Radeon RX 550 on a big-endian Power Mac G5
==========================================

Packages
--------
  linux-image-7.2.9+deb14-powerpc64-rx550g5
      Debian's 7.2.9 kernel configuration (built with GCC 13, so without BTF
      type information), with the big-endian amdgpu driver
      (command, MQD and ring byte order, display, VBIOS tables, HDMI/DP info
      packets, VCE ring wrap, soft recovery) and g5_cpu_temp. Stock Debian
      kernels stay installed as fallbacks in the GRUB "Advanced options" menu.
  libgl1-mesa-dri libglapi-mesa libegl-mesa0 libglx-mesa0 libgbm1
  mesa-va-drivers mesa-vdpau-drivers mesa-vulkan-drivers
      Mesa 24.1.6 with the big-endian GFX8 fixes, replacing the packages of
      the same names (version 24.1.6-1+rx550g5.N).
  rx550-g5 (this package)
      Boot integration, driver options, X configuration and an apt pin.

Install
-------
  sudo apt install ./*.deb      (all files from the release directory)
  sudo reboot

Keep the original graphics card (GeForce 6600 or similar) installed and
connected: the G5 firmware needs it to boot. The RX 550 drives the desktop.

On plain Debian (not MintPPC), whose Mesa is newer, add --allow-downgrades.

What this package does
----------------------
* Makes GRUB start the -rx550g5 kernel by default
  (/etc/default/grub.d/90-rx550-g5.cfg, removed with the package).
* rx550-g5.service loads amdgpu after boot and before the display manager.
  amdgpu is blacklisted for automatic loading so that a GPU problem can never
  stop the machine from booting: if a probe is interrupted (hang, crash,
  power loss), the record /var/lib/rx550-g5/probe-in-progress stops further
  automatic attempts. Delete it to try again.
* Driver options (/usr/lib/modprobe.d/rx550-g5.conf):
    runpm=0            keep the GPU powered (hotplug while suspended untested)
    gpu_recovery=0     full GPU reset fails on the G5; soft recovery
                       (killing a stuck shader) still runs
    lockup_timeout=10000  valid long jobs take more than the 2 s default
    ttm pages_limit=393216  GPU system memory goes through the 2 GB DART
                       window that SATA, network, USB and audio share; cap at
                       1.5 GB
* X: the modesetting driver with a software cursor for amdgpu devices
  (/usr/share/X11/xorg.conf.d/20-rx550-g5.conf). Files in
  /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d take precedence.
* An output connected after X started is switched on if nothing else is lit.
* /etc/apt/preferences.d/rx550-g5-mesa.pref keeps apt from replacing the Mesa
  packages with MintPPC's or Debian's builds.

Recovery
--------
* Append rx550.disable=1 to the kernel command line in GRUB (press e) to
  skip loading amdgpu, or pick a stock kernel under "Advanced options".
* sudo apt remove rx550-g5 restores the previous GRUB default. To return to
  stock Mesa, reinstall the distribution's packages, for example
  sudo apt install --allow-downgrades libgl1-mesa-dri=24.1.6-1 ... (MintPPC).

Video
-----
VA-API decode (H.264, HEVC 8/10-bit, MPEG-2) and VCE encode (H.264, HEVC)
were tested with ffmpeg. HEVC 10-bit frames are little-endian P010, which
ffmpeg labels p010be on this host, so converted output looks wrong although
the decoded bytes are right. ffmpeg reports no VA support for MPEG-4 part 2
and VP9 on this GPU. Mesa 26 has no VDPAU (removed upstream in 25.3); use VA-API.

OpenCL
------
mesa-opencl-icd (Rusticl on radeonsi) is included since 26.2.6-1+rx550g5.3; see
/usr/share/doc/libgl1-mesa-dri/README.rx550-g5. fp64 needs RUSTICL_FEATURES=fp64.

Not working or not tested
-------------------------
* Booting with the original card unplugged hangs the G5 firmware.
